      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Adora was over it. She had grown tired of years of back and forth, back and forth. Her sword was drawn; Catraâ€™s sharp claws were out, ready to pierce the heroineâ€™s skin. Adora tried to wipe her mind of Catra and every worry she brought. It was futile, her presence was ingrained into her mind. One she wanted gone and found, one she couldn't seem to let go.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catra couldn't get enough. One look into Adora's eyes and she spiraled, falling apart at the seams. Her brain muddled, her breath long gone as the realization dawned upon her, in all of its glory and to Catraâ€™s horror, she had only one thought.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If Adora wouldnâ€™t love her then hate was the next best thing.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
